      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits just east of Wheeler and northwest of Valparaiso, placing it within easy reach of the county seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_Creek_Commons%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A north‑flowing stream named Salt Creek borders the area, eventually joining the Little Calumet River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_Creek_Commons%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Salt Creek Valley Commons Homeowners Association, incorporated in 1975, governs the subdivision and maintains shared spaces.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/salt_creek_commons_indiana",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Housing stock largely consists of single‑family homes built between the late 1970s and early 1990s, with a median build year of 1979.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
